WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.685
What a working engineer would do.

2
00:00:01.965 --> 00:00:04.419
Write the decision down before you spend the money.

3
00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:21.488
A one-page note is enough: the eval set and the current score; the failures, classified as missing facts or wrong behavior; what you tried with prompting and retrieval and what each moved; the cost model at your expected volume, including dataset, training, serving,

4
00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:30.941
and the base model’s expected life; and the exit criteria, meaning the score a fine-tuned model must beat on the frozen test set, and by how much.

5
00:00:31.221 --> 00:00:32.736
That note does two jobs.

6
00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:39.267
It keeps the team from fine-tuning because it sounds like progress, and it gives you a baseline to beat when you do.

7
00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:52.581
The rest of this studio builds the pieces: this week the dataset, next week the training, and in week 4 an honest benchmark of your fine-tuned model against a frontier model on cost, latency, and accuracy.
